                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/1104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-31T13:00:00-03:00">December 31, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>355. Referring further to Department’s 215, December 20, 7 p.m. Decree signed
                    last night by President Vargas provides revisions of all Brazil’s trade
                    agreements except those concluded since January 1, 1934. Articles 3 and 5
                    provide definitely for the denunciation of the other agreements at dates to be
                    chosen in the discretion of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs but in such a manner
                    that all the agreements will cease to operate not later than July 30, 1936. Air
                    mail despatch follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
